<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Litovoi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Litovoi was a Romanian voivode of the 13th century whose land lay along the Jiu and Olt in what became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oltenia">Oltenia</a>, known from Hungarian royal charters. Béla IV's charter of 1247 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> left his knezate in Romanian hands, and a charter of 1285 says that a voivode Litovoi, perhaps the same man, refused tribute to Ladislaus IV around 1277–1279 and was killed by a royal army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/litovoi.jpg" alt="Litovoi" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: João do Cró · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LDAM_(f._025)_Rei_de_Blaqui.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
